From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:22:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v3d: hash shader-variant cache keys without a BLAKE3 per
 lookup

cache_hash() ran BLAKE3 over the variant key and the shader's stored BLAKE3
digest at every hash-table lookup, i.e. at every draw that changes state.
The table only needs a well-mixed 32-bit value and key->blake3 already is
a digest, so hash both with _mesa_hash_data()/_mesa_hash_data_with_seed().
The equality check is unchanged.

On a Raspberry Pi 4 the BLAKE3 was 5.1 % of SuperTuxKart's CPU in its menu.

Ported unchanged from a Mesa 26.2.x tree used by another operating
system port on the same board (Raspberry Pi 4, V3D 4.2). The numbers
below were measured there, not yet on Phoenix-RTOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_program.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_program.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_program.c
index f646383..f2df4fb 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_program.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_program.c
@@ -969,13 +969,13 @@ cache_hash(const void *_key, uint32_t key_size)
 {
         const struct v3d_cache_key *key = (struct v3d_cache_key *) _key;
 
-        blake3_hasher ctx;
-        unsigned char blake3[BLAKE3_KEY_LEN];
-        _mesa_blake3_init(&ctx);
-        _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, key->key, key_size);
-        _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, key->blake3, BLAKE3_KEY_LEN);
-        _mesa_blake3_final(&ctx, blake3);
-        return _mesa_hash_data(blake3, BLAKE3_KEY_LEN);
+        /* The hash table only needs a well-mixed 32-bit value: key->blake3 is
+         * already a digest of the shader, so hash it and the variant key with
+         * the table's own hash instead of a BLAKE3 at every lookup (a variant
+         * lookup runs at every draw that changes state).
+         */
+        uint32_t hash = _mesa_hash_data(key->blake3, BLAKE3_KEY_LEN);
+        return _mesa_hash_data_with_seed(key->key, key_size, hash);
 }
 
 static inline bool
